    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5504" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bocchus</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a king of
			Mauritania</i>, <i>father-in-law of Jugurtha</i>, <i>whom he gave up bound to Sulla</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. J.
				19, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">80</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">81</span></i>; 83; 97; 101
			sqq.; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2, 12, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Max.
				8, 14, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 1, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 5,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 2, 1, § 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 5, 5, §
			15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>, <i>so called in honor of
				him</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βώχ, βοτάνης
			εἶδος</span>, Hesych.; <i><span class="en">Verg. Cul.
			404</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A king of Mauritania</i>, <i>son of
				the former</i>, Auct. B. Afr 25.</div>
